<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Some bids rolled to Sept.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Some bids rolled to Sept.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash bids in Minneapolis for dark northern spring wheat were rolled Thursday from the July to the September spring wheat contract at the Minneapolis Grain Exchange.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis switched to the September option on Thursday,&quot; USDA's Market News said in its weekly grain summary from Minneapolis. Market News also reported milling demand for spring wheat was light Thursday.</p>
<p>MGE September wheat settled up nine cents per bushel in mostly light volume. Other months were five to 9-1/2 cents per bushel higher.  </p>
